// Test: a QUERY-ROOTED resolver whose `@rootFragment` reads server data but which
// does NOT declare `@returnFragment` is currently EXCLUDED from
// `has_server_to_client_resolvers`.
//
// This pins a known gap, not desired behaviour. `build_ast.rs` decides the flag with
//
//     Some(parent_type) != self.schema.query_type()
//         || resolver_metadata.return_fragment.is_some()
//
// so a Query parent only qualifies via the magic-fragment carve-out. The exclusion
// exists because a Query-rooted resolver normally reads only client state; the
// carve-out was added for magic fragments, whose transplant puts server selections
// into the operation. A resolver that reads server data through a plain
// `@rootFragment` crosses exactly the same boundary and is still excluded — the
// comment in `build_ast.rs` says so.
//
// Why it matters: without the flag, `LSRelayEnvironmentConfig` never routes the
// operation to `executeWithNetwork`. It lands on the legacy path, where the resolver
// and the network run as two concurrent subscriptions and the root fragment is
// evaluated against an empty store — silently yielding null.
//
// It has not bitten yet only because every Query-rooted shadow resolver we ship IS a
// magic fragment, so the carve-out covers it.
//
// EXPECTED IN THE GOLDEN: `NeedsRoutingQuery` must NOT contain
// `has_server_to_client_resolvers`.
//
// The fix is already available and this fixture is what will catch it landing. The
// compiler ALREADY emits `hasServerField` on a resolver root fragment that reaches a
// server field — see the `resolver_root_fragment_has_server_field` fixture — which is
// exactly the predicate the routing flag should key on instead of `@returnFragment`.
// (That signal is not shown here because emitting a split operation needs
// `resolversSchemaModule`, which this minimal schema cannot register.) When the flag
// switches to it, this fixture must be updated rather than passing silently.

//- NeedsRoutingQuery.js
graphql`query NeedsRoutingQuery @exec_time_resolvers {
  server_reading_greeting
}`

//- Query_server_reading_greeting.js
/**
 * @relayField Query.server_reading_greeting: String
 * @rootFragment QueryServerReadingGreetingFragment
 */
graphql`fragment QueryServerReadingGreetingFragment on Query {
  me {
    name
  }
}`

//- relay.config.json
{
  "language": "typescript",
  "schema": "schema.graphql",
  "featureFlags": {
    "enable_exec_time_resolvers_directive": true
  }
}

//- schema.graphql
type Query {
  me: User
}

type User {
  name: String
}
